2026-06-06 19:48:33,711 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Q1: What files are present on RM3?
2026-06-06 19:48:33,712 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] RM3 contains at least one large DOCX document from the digitalcorpora.org GovDocs corpus, focused on U.S. government IT governance (FEA Reference Model, OMB circulars, Library of Congress catalog entries). The document contains 44+ embedded images (Kodak DC260/DX4530 photos, Adobe Photoshop CS graphics, Corbis stock photos). Contact information for wayne.longman@att.net, Eric_P._Lauer@omb.eop.gov, and mmun@loc.gov is embedded within the document content. Crucially, IREAP/UMER references from the "Secret Project" documents also appear on RM3.
2026-06-06 19:48:33,714 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Q2: Are there deleted or recoverable files?
2026-06-06 19:48:33,715 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **No.** PhotoRec recovered 0 files. CD-ROM is read-only media — files cannot be deleted post-burn. TSK fls could not list files due to UDF filesystem limitations.
2026-06-06 19:48:33,717 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Q3: What metadata is in the documents?
2026-06-06 19:48:33,717 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] Document images were processed on **Apple Macintosh** using **Adobe Photoshop CS Macintosh** (11 images, all dated 2006-03-21). Camera photos from **Kodak DC260** (2003) and **Kodak DX4530** (2004). Corbis stock photos (2008-2009) with Microsoft Corporation attribution. Image creation spans 2003–2009.
2026-06-06 19:48:33,725 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Q4: What is the file timeline?
2026-06-06 19:48:33,727 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] The ISO image was created **2015-03-26 at 18:35:29 UTC**, one day after the final anti-forensics cleanup on the source PC (March 24-25). Embedded content dates span 2003-2009 (pre-existing government documents).
2026-06-06 19:48:33,729 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Q5: Is there hidden, encrypted, or steganographic content?
2026-06-06 19:48:33,729 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **No.** Steganography detection returned negative. YARA scanning with ~4,000 rules produced no matches. No encryption detected.
