2026-06-06 20:19:42,515 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q9: Does the Outlook OST file (iaman.informant@nist.gov.ost, inode 46112) contain Secret Project documents as email attachments or evidence of coordination with external recipients? The suspect researched 'e-mail investigation' and 'Forensic Email Investigation' (88 and 78 hits respectively), suggesting awareness that email would be examined.",
2026-06-06 20:19:42,515 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q10: What browser history timestamps correspond to the anti-forensics research queries? Bulk_extractor carved search terms but not visit dates — browser SQLite databases can pinpoint when the suspect researched 'anti-forensic tools', 'how to leak a secret', and 'security checkpoint cd-r'.",
2026-06-06 20:19:42,516 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q11: Do Shellbags or Jump Lists record the user navigating Secret Project file paths on the PC or USB? These artifacts survive CCleaner cleanup in many cases and would prove the user accessed the documents on the local machine.",
2026-06-06 20:19:42,517 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q12: Do LNK files contain USB volume serial numbers matching RM1 (5c75-4d3e) or RM2 device identifiers, linking specific file access to specific USB devices?",
2026-06-06 20:19:42,517 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] "Q13: Is the content on RM3 (CD-ROM) a duplicate of RM1/RM2 documents, or does it contain additional exfiltrated data? The IREAP/UMER references match, but file-level comparison requires UDF extraction which TSK cannot perform."
